    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Will Smith** (67.82) and **Zack Gelof** (66.52) anchor our lineup, boasting the highest efficiency scores due to prime lineup placement and favorable matchups against Michael King and Yusei Kikuchi, respectively. **Will Smith** is a high-floor play despite his lineup status remaining pending, benefiting from a high xwOBA and an advantageous spot in the order. **Zack Gelof** represents our most compelling situational play; while facing a left-handed arm in Kikuchi typically draws concern, his +10% park factor and +7% platoon advantage override the marginal drag of facing an elite-delivery catcher, making him a primary source of production. **Bryce Harper** (62.71) remains an elite start against Dustin May, carrying high raw value that mitigates the moderate headwind risk in today\u2019s park environment.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks, most notably the \"Wind In\" warnings impacting **Luis Arraez**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Jonathan Aranda**, which suppressed their ceiling projections. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an essential start given his pedigree, his score was tempered by a -17% adjustment against a tougher matchup versus Payton Tolle. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Kyle Karros** (48.80); he was the closest consideration for the final utility spot, but his lower base projection relative to **Jonathan Aranda** and the general volatility of his current platoon split kept him on the pine. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Daulton Varsho** (48.96); his value is highly sensitive to his slotting against Logan Gilbert, but his +10% dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed starter keeps him marginally ahead of the replacement threshold.",
